<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Cumnock Coal says chairman resigns.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Cumnock Coal says chairman resigns.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cumnock Coal Ltd said on Wednesday that chairman and managing director Tom Johnson had resigned.</p>
<p>His replacement was not named.</p>
<p>Swiss-based metals house Glencore AG holds about 25 percent of Cumnock, which was talked of as a takeover target earlier this year after discussions with CIM Resources Ltd.</p>
<p>CIM said on September 26 that it had lost interest in Cumnock due to Glencore's attitude.</p>
<p>Cumnock shares closed untraded but were bid at A$2.30, unchanged from its previous close.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
